==English==
{{was wotd|2018|June|16}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*wenh₁-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|wynsom}}, {{m|enm|winsom}}, {{m|enm|winsome}}, {{m|enm|winsum}}, {{m|enm|wunsum|t=beautiful; agreeable, gracious, pleasant; generous; of situations: favourable, propitious}}, from {{inh|en|ang|wynsum|t=joyful, merry, pleasant; winsome}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*wunnjusam|t=joyful}}; synchronically analyzable as {{suf|en|winne|t1=delight, joy, pleasure|some}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈwɪn.s(ə)m/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈwɪn.səm/}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-winsome.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{hyphenation|en|win|some}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# [[charming#Adjective|Charming]], [[engaging#Adjective|engaging]], [[winning#Adjective|winning]]; [[inspire|inspiring]] [[approval]] and [[trust#Noun|trust]], especially if in an [[innocent#Adjective|innocent]] manner.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1847|author=[[w:Emily Brontë|Emily Brontë]]|title=Wuthering Heights|url=https://www.gutenberg.org/files/768/768-h/768-h.htm|chapter=IX
|passage={{...}} lifting her '''winsome''' eyes to my face with that sort of look which turns off bad temper, even when one has all the right in the world to indulge it.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Jonathan Freke Slingsby [pseudonym; {{w|John Francis Waller}}]|title=Slingsby in Scotland. Part II.—Conclusion.|magazine=[[w:Dublin University Magazine|The Dublin University Magazine, a Literary and Political Journal]]|location=Dublin|publisher=[[w:Gill (publisher)|James McGlashan]], 50 [[w:O'Connell Street|Upper Sackville-St.]]; London: W[illia]m S[omerville] Orr|month=October|year=1851|volume=XXXVIII|number=CCXXVI|section=stanza I|page=494|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=rJk6AQAAMAAJ&pg=PA494|oclc=841086102|passage=Will ye keep your troth to me, / '''Winsome''' Annie Ramsay? / Will ye keep your troth to me, / '''Winsome''' Annie Ramsay? / Will ye keep your troth to me? / My ain true luve will ye be? / Then meet me at the trysting tree, / '''Winsome''' Annie Ramsay.}}
#* {{RQ:Joyce Ulysses|chapter=Episode 13, Nausicaa|page=333|passage=Gerty MacDowell who was seated near her companions, lost in thought, gazing far away into the distance was in very truth as fair a specimen of '''winsome''' Irish girlhood as one could wish to see.}}
#* {{RQ:Song Chinese in Singapore|chapter=XI|page=377|format=full|passage=He [Ching Keng Lee] is a man of fine physique and above the height of the average Straits-born, with a shrewd business head, and affable and '''winsome''' manners, and continues to take a keen interest in public affairs.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=David Alexander|chapter=When the Rain Stops|title=Hangman’s Dozen|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=Roy Publishers|year=1961|page=216|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=klZRAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA216|oclc=1118558|passage=The pink wallpaper of the nursery was decorated with a Noah's Ark of friendly lions and comical giraffes and '''winsome''' elephants.}}

